            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for a security guard, then the Marathi for to bring under control."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अडथळा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अडथळा — aḍthaḷā — \"an obstacle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रस्त्यात पडलेलं झाड हा मोठा अडथळा होता. rastyāt paḍlelaṁ jhāḍ hā moṭhā aḍthaḷā hotā. The tree lying on the road was a big obstacle."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अडथळा (aḍthaḷā) begins with अड, \"obstruction\": CDIAL lists Marathi aḍ, \"obstruction\", and aḍṇẽ, \"to be stopped\", under aḍ, \"obstruct, stop\" (CDIAL 187). The second part is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
